            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A method of producing a liquid tobacco extract comprises the steps of: preparing a tobacco starting material; heating the tobacco starting material in a flow of inert gas at an extraction temperature of between 125 degrees Celsius and 160 degrees Celsius for between 90 minutes and 270 minutes; collecting the volatile compounds released from the tobacco starting material during the heating step, wherein the volatile compounds are collected by condensation; and forming a liquid tobacco extract comprising the collected volatile compounds.</p>
            </abstract>
